{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1340354-red-surrrender-how-does-it-fit-or-not-in-2nd-edition","id":1340354,"title":"Red Surrrender, how does it fit or not in 2nd edition?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-10-08T20:33:19-07:00","id":1340354,"title":"Red Surrrender, how does it fit or not in 2nd edition?","content":"Hello people, it has been years since i actually played or STed Requiem, all of it in late 1e, so pardon the utter greeness of my doubts and questions.<br /> <br /> <br /> Subject is pretty much what says in the title - is the Red Surrrender still sound (so to speak) as a concept or something made obsolete by current takes on kindred interaction with the Beast?<br /> <br /> If the concept is viable still, does it call for tweaking? Of what kind would you suggest? And how might the &quot;Rumor of Defiance/Surrender Rebuke&quot; fit in?<br /> <br /> Like something out of torpor, trying to get up to date again before getting fully back into action. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-08-2019, 11:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-09T03:48:00-07:00","id":1340387,"title":"","content":"I think it can work fine as a set of Conditions. I don't see any good reason why it can't be ported over and used.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-09T05:59:02-07:00","id":1340398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1340354-red-surrrender-how-does-it-fit-or-not-in-2nd-edition?p=1340387#post1340387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it can work fine as a set of Conditions. I don't see any good reason why it can't be ported over and used.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Good to know. Condition sets is one of those things i need to get a better hang of anyway, so it's a kind of &quot;two birds, one stone&quot; , i guess. Conditions then. As good a place to start as any.<br /> <br /> Would like to hear of other people's experiences with using the Red Surrender on either 1e or 2e games, but that's for when it comes up (or not).<br /> Also, do any othe 2e books discusses draugr and/or larvae? Somewhat related i guess.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-10T02:49:44-07:00","id":1340588,"title":"","content":"A lot of the design space for them is taken over by revenants, which are described most widely in Half Damned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-10T05:50:42-07:00","id":1340603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1340354-red-surrrender-how-does-it-fit-or-not-in-2nd-edition?p=1340588#post1340588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lot of the design space for them is taken over by revenants, which are described most widely in Half Damned.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hmmm, revenants, i have heard of them. More limited and miserable than the average neonate but all too human in their condition unlike feral larvae &amp; draugr, at least afaik. I keep forgetting about these many micro-changes here and there to the vampiric condition they made between the two editions. That's something else to get the hang of how it maps out in the table, i guess.<br /> <br /> But then, it's not like the Surrender, draugr and larvae were in the game from day one either.<br /> Sometimes makes me think of cooking some &quot;lost clans&quot; or somesuch just to mess with abandoned weaknesses, discipline powers and other small bits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-10-2019, 09:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}